<title>ITALY: SOCCER-ITALY COACH MALDINI'S CAREER PATH.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ITALY COACH MALDINI'S CAREER PATH.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are brief career</p>
<p>highlights of new Italy coach Cesare Maldini:</p>
<p>February 5, 1932 - Born Trieste, north-eastern Italy</p>
<p>1953 - Signed for Triestina</p>
<p>May 24, 1953 - Makes league debut for Triestina, a 0-0 draw</p>
<p>against Palermo</p>
<p>1954 - Joins AC Milan</p>
<p>1955 - Milan win league title</p>
<p>1957 - Milan win league title</p>
<p>1959 - Milan win league title</p>
<p>January 6, 1960 - Wins first cap for Italy in Naples. Italy</p>
<p>beat Switzerland 3-0.</p>
<p>November 11, 1962 - Becomes Italy captain. Italy beat</p>
<p>Austria 2-1 in friendly in Vienna.</p>
<p>1962 - Milan win league title</p>
<p>May 22, 1963 - Milan beat Benfica 2-1 in European Cup final</p>
<p>at Wembley. Maldini is the captain.</p>
<p>October 13, 1963 - Maldini plays last match for Italy,</p>
<p>against Russia in Moscow. Italy lose 2-0.</p>
<p>1966 - Moves to Torino</p>
<p>May 28, 1967 - Last serie A match, for Torino</p>
<p>June 26, 1968 - Son Paolo born.</p>
<p>1971 - Joins technical staff at AC Milan</p>
<p>1974 - Coach of Foggia (dismissed in 1975)</p>
<p>1976 - Coach of Ternana (to 1977)</p>
<p>1979 - Takes Parma from serie C to serie B.</p>
<p>1980 - Dismissed by Parma</p>
<p>1980 - Becomes deputy to national coach Enzo Bearzot.</p>
<p>1982 - Italy win the World Cup</p>
<p>1986 - Becomes Italian under-21 coach, after accompanying</p>
<p>Bearzot to Mexico World Cup</p>
<p>1992 - Italy win European under-21 championship</p>
<p>1994 - Italy win European under-21 championship</p>
<p>1996 - Italy win European under-21 championship</p>
<p>December 15, 1996 - Appointed Italy coach</p>
</text>
